  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Hydrocodone is a powerful, habit-forming opioid painkiller used to treat severe pain, often combined with acetaminophen (e.g., Vicodin, Norco). It works by changing how the brain responds to pain but carries risks of addiction, misuse, and fatal respiratory depression. Common side effects include dizziness, constipation, and nausea. Common Uses Pain Management: Used to treat severe pain that cannot be managed with other, non-opioid medications. Combination Drugs: Frequently combined with non-opioid pain relievers like acetaminophen to enhance pain relief. Common Brand Names Vicodin Norco Lortab Lorcet Hycodan Vicoprofen Common Side Effects Dizziness or lightheadedness Constipation Nausea and vomiting Drowsiness Dry mouth Headache Overdose SymptomsOverdose can be fatal and requires immediate emergency help (call 911). Symptoms include: Slowed or stopped breathing Extreme drowsiness or sluggishness Loss of muscle tone Cold, clammy skin Pinpoint pupils Coma Withdrawal SymptomsStopping the medication suddenly can cause severe withdrawal. Symptoms include: Restlessness or irritability Muscle aches and backache Joint pain Insomnia Diarrhea, vomiting, or cold flashes Warnings Addiction and Dependence: Long-term use can lead to physical and mental dependence. Respiratory Depression: Serious, life-threatening breathing issues can occur. Alcohol Interaction: Do not drink alcohol or take alcohol-containing products, as this increases the risk of dangerous side effects, including death. Fatal Misuse: Never share this medication. It can be fatal to others, especially children. Storage: Keep in a secure place, out of reach of children. For a detailed overview of side effects and warning signs, consult a medical professional or visit MedlinePlus. MedlinePlus",
